{"id": 17, "ts": 1780599540.5914767, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s reliability and quick decision\u2011making, but we still have no concrete evidence that C can stay calm under the high\u2011pressure, long\u2011haul scenarios that define this role. Sarah confirmed there are no explicit observations on C\u2019s stress resilience, and the only technical note is his ability to make correct decisions quickly, which doesn\u2019t fully address the broader cognitive and system\u2011knowledge demands of a long\u2011distance pilot.\nConversely, James highlighted that Candidate\u202fB \u201chandles stress very well,\u201d giving us a clear indicator of stress resilience. While B\u2019s relatively weak memory for numbers is noted, James has no specific examples of this causing operational errors, so the risk remains unproven. Given that stress resilience is a non\u2011negotiable safety criterion, I am inclined to favor the candidate with documented strength in that area. Therefore, I would move my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fB**."}
